# Deliberately empty, for the WEB build only.
#
# main.py serves the web bundle from the same origin as the API, so a relative
# base is correct there — and it has to be relative, because production CORS is
# same-origin only. Baking the absolute backend URL in here would make the web
# app call itself cross-origin and get blocked.
#
# Native builds are the opposite: an APK has no origin, so a relative base
# resolves to the phone itself. They take the absolute URL from eas.json's
# `env`, which wins over this file because real environment variables take
# precedence over .env entries.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
